Package: SPMD
Title: Symmetric Pair Matching Design for Causal Inference
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Robin", "Denz", , "robin.denz@rub.de", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Maintainer: Robin Denz <robin.denz@rub.de>
Description: Symmetric pair matching is a self-controlled method that is designed to
	allow estimation of the causal effect of a transient exposure (such as vaccinations) on a potentially recurrent outcome.
	It automatically adjust for all time-invariant confounders and time effects using a special kind of pair matching. As such,
	only very minimal assumptions have to be made about how time influences the exposure or outcome probability.
	See Denz et al. (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2608.25979> for more information.
